2026-10-14  Ne10+ + H CTMC (Schultz 2014; Cumbee et al. 2016) ne10+h_sec_ctmc.cs: n = 16-20 added
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The file kept n <= 15 although its Total is the full CTMC total, so its states summed to 0-2.2 % less than the total (2.2 % at
50 keV/u). The 65 states 16s-20y added from the authors' per-energy CTMC output (n <= 15 equal to the file); existing numbers
and Total unchanged. The remaining gap (states 0.989-1.000 of Total; 1.1 % at 50 keV/u) is capture into n > 20, counted in the
CTMC total but not listed by n in the author files. radrathe.dat reaches n = 20. Header line 6 notes it. Script
Working/Theory/AdaptToKronos/ne10h_ctmc_add_n16_20_20261014.py; originals in AdaptToKronos/ne10h_ctmc_before_n16_20_20261014-001702.tgz.
Files: CXDatabase/Projectile_Ions/Ne/Charge/10/Targets/H/ne10+h_sec_ctmc.cs

2026-10-13  O7+ + H (Nolte et al., unpublished) o7+h_sec_qmocc.cs -> o7+h_sec_rcmd.cs, rebuilt from the authors' original rec files: 0.01 eV/u - 200 keV/u
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The 2016 file was made from copies of the authors' recommended files (*_rec.dat, Stancil group) thinned to the Kronos energies.
