2026-10-13  C5+ + H Nolte et al. 2012: c5+h_sec_qmocc.cs renamed c5+h_sec_rcmd.cs (recommended QMOCC/AOCC set)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The file is a recommended set, not QMOCC throughout (user decision): 100-1000 eV/u QMOCC (n = 3, 4; the paper's QMOCC goes down to
0.01 eV/u, not in the file), 10-200 keV/u the one-electron AOCC split 1:3 singlet:triplet (n = 2-7), 1.5-7 keV/u a join of the two.
Renamed to *_sec_rcmd.cs; header line 4 Method=QMOCC -> Method=QMOCC/AOCC (as o6+h_sec_rcmd.cs); line 6 notes the composition.
Data unchanged. Script Working/Theory/AdaptToKronos/rename_c5h_qmocc_to_rcmd_20261013.py; original in
AdaptToKronos/c5h_qmocc_before_rcmd_rename_20261013-211959.tgz.
Files: CXDatabase/Projectile_Ions/C/Charge/5/Targets/H/c5+h_sec_qmocc.cs (removed) -> CXDatabase/Projectile_Ions/C/Charge/5/Targets/H/c5+h_sec_rcmd.cs

